Chapter: ClipBpeForge
  cites AI chapter ClipBpe
  cites Foreword chapter FactDisk

 The disk is build/mint-clip-bpe-disk.ps1's: a header sector holding the two
 file lengths, then vocab.json and merges.txt unmodified. Every id line of the
 .expected is build/clip-bpe-oracle.py's output, the ids Diffusion Forge's
 own CLIPTokenizer gives the same strings. The first is Diffusion.md's stage
 4a grade, the next nine are generate-art.ps1's eight prompts behind its style
 prefix and its negative prompt, and the last four aim at contractions,
 digits and punctuation runs, the special tokens, and characters above ASCII.

 We say:

